WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Look closely.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.850
C, small o.

3
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.610
And C, capital O.

4
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.210
Almost the same, right?

5
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.670
But C small o is cobalt: a metal.

6
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.430
C capital O isn't an element at all.

7
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.370
It's carbon and oxygen,
joined together.

8
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.570
One small letter changes everything.

9
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.530
Scientists all over the
world read this code.

10
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.270
In this mission, you'll
learn it: symbols, formulae,

11
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.870
and the small numbers
that count atoms.

12
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.270
Then you'll follow a
reaction, atom by atom.

13
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.430
When methane burns, do
any atoms disappear?

14
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.930
Do new ones appear?

15
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.210
Your mission: prove what happens
to every atom in a reaction.
